# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Rangkai Book Metadata - Environment Variables Template
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your actual values
# NEVER commit `.env` to version control
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Better Auth Configuration (v2.0+)                           │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Base URL for authentication callbacks
# Development: http://localhost:5173
# Production: https://your-domain.com
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Google OAuth Credentials (REQUIRED for v2.0+)               │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
# Get these from: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 
# Steps to get Google OAuth credentials:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com
# 2. Create a new project or select existing project
# 3. Navigate to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials"
# 4. Click "Create Credentials" > "OAuth client ID"
# 5. Application type: "Web application"
# 6. Authorized redirect URIs:
#    - Development: http://localhost:5173/api/auth/callback/google
#    - Production: https://your-domain.com/api/auth/callback/google
# 7. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret below

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret-here

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Optional: Google Books API (v1.x legacy)                    │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
# Only needed if you want to increase Google Books API quota
# Default public API usage works without a key

# GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=your_key_here

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Cloudflare Configuration (Production Only)                  │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
# These are automatically injected by Cloudflare Pages
# Configure in wrangler.toml for local development with Wrangler
#
# Cloudflare D1 Database: rangkai-scans
# Cloudflare KV Namespace: BOOK_CACHE
#
# Note: Local development uses Wrangler to emulate D1 and KV
# Production deployment uses actual Cloudflare services

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Optional: Development Settings                              │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Enable debug logging (default: false)
# DEBUG=true

# Node environment (default: development)
# NODE_ENV=development

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 🔒 SECURITY NOTES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# - NEVER commit `.env` to version control (already in .gitignore)
# - Rotate secrets regularly (especially GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET)
# - Use different credentials for dev/staging/production
# - Store production secrets in Cloudflare Pages Environment Variables:
#   https://dash.cloudflare.com → Pages → rangkai-book-metadata → Settings → Environment variables
# - Enable 2FA on Google Cloud Console account
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

